Relevant columns for “highest season goals of each team”

• Match."home_team_api_id" / Match."away_team_api_id" : team identifier in every match  
• Match."season" : the season string (e.g. “2012/2013”) to aggregate by season  
• Match."home_team_goal" / Match."away_team_goal" : goals scored by the team in the match  
• Team."team_api_id" : key to obtain the long/short team names (optional, for readability)

Typical conditions you are likely to need  
• Ignore rows whose goal columns are NULL → WHERE "home_team_goal" IS NOT NULL …  
• Exclude matches whose team id is NULL (some rare rows)  
• Because the same team appears twice (home & away), aggregate the two goal columns separately and UNION ALL them before summing.  

Below are ten exploratory → analytic SQL statements (each limited to 20 rows where meaningful) that gradually build up to the final answer – the median of every team’s best‑ever seasonal goal total.

```sql
-- 1. Distinct list of seasons that exist in the Match table
SELECT DISTINCT "season"
FROM "Match"
ORDER BY "season"
LIMIT 20;

-- 2. Sample of team ids that appear as the home side
SELECT DISTINCT "home_team_api_id"
FROM "Match"
WHERE "home_team_api_id" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;

-- 3. Quick look at goals recorded in raw match rows
SELECT "id", "season", "home_team_api_id", "away_team_api_id",
       "home_team_goal", "away_team_goal"
FROM "Match"
WHERE "home_team_goal" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;

-- 4. Peek at team names that correspond to the ids
SELECT "team_api_id", "team_long_name"
FROM "Team"
ORDER BY "team_api_id"
LIMIT 20;

-- 5. Total goals a chosen team (e.g. 9987) scored in every season (home + away merged)
WITH single_team AS (
  SELECT "season", SUM("home_team_goal") AS goals
  FROM "Match"
  WHERE "home_team_api_id" = 9987
  GROUP BY "season"
  UNION ALL
  SELECT "season", SUM("away_team_goal")
  FROM "Match"
  WHERE "away_team_api_id" = 9987
  GROUP BY "season"
)
SELECT "season", SUM(goals) AS total_goals
FROM single_team
GROUP BY "season"
ORDER BY total_goals DESC
LIMIT 20;

-- 6. For every team: total goals in every season (two separate aggregations then merged)
WITH team_season AS (
  SELECT "home_team_api_id" AS team_id,
         "season",
         SUM("home_team_goal") AS goals
  FROM "Match"
  WHERE "home_team_goal" IS NOT NULL
  GROUP BY team_id, "season"
  UNION ALL
  SELECT "away_team_api_id",
         "season",
         SUM("away_team_goal")
  FROM "Match"
  WHERE "away_team_goal" IS NOT NULL
  GROUP BY "away_team_api_id", "season"
)
SELECT team_id, "season", SUM(goals) AS season_goals
FROM team_season
GROUP BY team_id, "season"
ORDER BY season_goals DESC
LIMIT 20;

-- 7. Highest‑scoring season for each team
WITH team_season_agg AS (
  SELECT team_id, "season", SUM(goals) AS season_goals
  FROM (
        SELECT "home_team_api_id" AS team_id, "season", "home_team_goal" AS goals
        FROM "Match"
        UNION ALL
        SELECT "away_team_api_id", "season", "away_team_goal"
        FROM "Match"
       )
  GROUP BY team_id, "season"
)
SELECT team_id,
       MAX(season_goals) AS highest_season_goals
FROM team_season_agg
GROUP BY team_id
ORDER BY highest_season_goals DESC
LIMIT 20;

-- 8. Same result as #7 but with team names attached
WITH team_season_agg AS (
  SELECT team_id, "season", SUM(goals) AS season_goals
  FROM (
        SELECT "home_team_api_id" AS team_id, "season", "home_team_goal" AS goals
        FROM "Match"
        UNION ALL
        SELECT "away_team_api_id", "season", "away_team_goal"
        FROM "Match"
       )
  GROUP BY team_id, "season"
),
team_best AS (
  SELECT team_id, MAX(season_goals) AS best_goals
  FROM team_season_agg
  GROUP BY team_id
)
SELECT t."team_long_name", tb.best_goals
FROM team_best tb
JOIN "Team" t
  ON t."team_api_id" = tb.team_id
ORDER BY tb.best_goals DESC
LIMIT 20;

-- 9. Ordered list of every team’s best‑ever seasonal total (needed for median)
WITH team_season_agg AS (
  SELECT team_id, "season", SUM(goals) AS season_goals
  FROM (
        SELECT "home_team_api_id" AS team_id, "season", "home_team_goal" AS goals
        FROM "Match"
        UNION ALL
        SELECT "away_team_api_id", "season", "away_team_goal"
        FROM "Match"
       )
  GROUP BY team_id, "season"
),
team_best AS (
  SELECT team_id, MAX(season_goals) AS best_goals
  FROM team_season_agg
  GROUP BY team_id
)
SELECT best_goals
FROM team_best
ORDER BY best_goals
LIMIT 20;

-- 10. FINAL ANSWER  – median of all teams’ best‑ever seasonal goal totals
WITH team_season AS (
  SELECT "home_team_api_id" AS team_id,
         "season",
         SUM("home_team_goal") AS goals
  FROM "Match"
  GROUP BY team_id, "season"
  UNION ALL
  SELECT "away_team_api_id",
         "season",
         SUM("away_team_goal")
  FROM "Match"
  GROUP BY "away_team_api_id", "season"
),
team_best AS (
  SELECT team_id, MAX(goals) AS best_goals
  FROM team_season
  GROUP BY team_id
),
ordered AS (
  SELECT best_goals,
         ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY best_goals) AS rn,
         COUNT(*)  OVER ()                             AS cnt
  FROM team_best
)
SELECT AVG(best_goals) AS median_best_season_goals
FROM ordered
WHERE rn IN ( (cnt + 1) / 2, (cnt + 2) / 2 );
```

Each query incrementally explores or computes a portion of the information, culminating in the tenth statement, which returns the median value of the highest seasonal goal tallies achieved by every team in the dataset.
